+<aside class="notes"><b>s29 · REPLACES s29</b><p>Point first to the completed read transaction, then storage verification outside row locks. The adoption transaction locks/rechecks the reservation, pins the exact version, creates Asset and stages MediaOutbox through enqueue_submit. The function returns Asset to api.uploads.finalize_upload, which returns Accepted with HTTP 202. Replay returns the prior Asset without a second submit; expiry or verification failure prevents adoption.</p><p>Sequence aliases: s=session, f=factory, cfg=settings, t=transport, e=envelope, jid/aid=Job/Attempt UUID, rid=reservation UUID, k=new source key, dir=temporary directory, work=Claim. These denote values passed to real signatures. SQL-prefixed labels summarize persistence effects; they are not invented AsyncSession methods. Filled arrows show synchronous/awaited calls, open arrows show asynchronous delivery, dashed arrows show replies; module lifelines denote the named real module, not an OO service.</p><p>Verified source: <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/api/uploads.py#L36">media/api/uploads.py#L36</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/direct_intake.py#L99">media/services/direct_intake.py#L99</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/direct_intake.py#L149">media/services/direct_intake.py#L149</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/storage.py#L62">media/services/storage.py#L62</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/messaging.py#L31">media/messaging.py#L31</a></p></aside>
