+<h1 style="font-size:40px">Editing commits a new Asset before SQS</h1>
+<div style="font:600 15px Menlo,monospace;color:#64748b;margin:-10px 0 8px">SAD · SDP · Edit object interaction</div>
+<div class="body" style="margin-bottom:44px"><img src="assets/uml/W3-14-edit.svg" alt="Edit stages a derived Asset and submit intent before later relay" style="max-width:1180px;max-height:535px;display:block;margin:0 auto"></div>
+<div class="sec">4. Detailed design</div>
+<div class="foot"><span><a class="pl" href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/api/v1_jobs.py#L55" target="_blank" rel="noopener">media/api/v1_jobs.py#L55</a> · <a class="pl" href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L105" target="_blank" rel="noopener">media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L105</a></span><span>W3-05 · 76282d3</span></div>
+<aside class="notes"><b>s30 · REPLACES s30</b><p>Read the new-edit success path. v1_jobs.edit is the caller; replay returns the prior Asset before parent validation. A new edit requires an owned, nondeleted parent, a done projection and primary output. intake.stage commits the StagedObject ledger. Copy holds the parent/staged locks; Storage streams GET/hash/tempfile/PUT, then the copy transaction records write_uncertain=False. Adoption locks/checks the staged row, inserts the derived Asset (source_asset_id=parent_id), pins VersionId/SourceVersion through the wrapper, stages the submit outbox and removes the staged ledger in one commit. pinning performs storage verification inside adoption. The figure summarizes SQL effects; W3-14b expands them. The later scheduled relay is W3-14a in backup. SQS publication follows adoption commit; the schedule can race the HTTP response, so wall-clock 202-before-send ordering is not guaranteed. Failures call discard_stage; a concurrent RequestKey loser discards its copy and replays the winner.</p><p>Sequence aliases: s=session, f=factory, cfg=settings, t=transport, e=envelope, jid/aid=Job/Attempt UUID, rid=reservation UUID, k=new source key, dir=temporary directory, work=Claim. These denote values passed to real signatures. SQL-prefixed labels summarize persistence effects; they are not invented AsyncSession methods. Filled arrows show synchronous/awaited calls, open arrows show asynchronous delivery, dashed arrows show replies; module lifelines denote the named real module, not an OO service.</p><p>Verified source: <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/api/v1_jobs.py#L55">media/api/v1_jobs.py#L55</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L105">media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L105</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L145">media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L145</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/direct_intake.py#L75">media/services/direct_intake.py#L75</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/storage.py#L209">media/services/storage.py#L209</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/intake.py#L54">media/services/intake.py#L54</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/handlers.py#L70">media/handlers.py#L70</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/delivery/sql.py#L58">delivery/sql.py#L58</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/scripts/aws/v1/definitions.py#L1766">scripts/aws/v1/definitions.py#L1766</a></p></aside>
