+<aside class="notes"><b>w3-stale · NEW after s31</b><p>The caller is worker.sqs carrying work:Claim, not a Claim object making a method call. Assume descriptor validation succeeds first. Inside lock_pair the locked Job names A2, so it returns None. DB-clock live(None,T1,now) is False. The transaction makes no state/outbox change; False returns through messaging to worker. Media separately checks delayed snapshot version/attempt fences in W3-13a.</p><p>Sequence aliases: s=session, f=factory, cfg=settings, t=transport, e=envelope, jid/aid=Job/Attempt UUID, rid=reservation UUID, k=new source key, dir=temporary directory, work=Claim. These denote values passed to real signatures. SQL-prefixed labels summarize persistence effects; they are not invented AsyncSession methods. Filled arrows show synchronous/awaited calls, open arrows show asynchronous delivery, dashed arrows show replies; module lifelines denote the named real module, not an OO service.</p><p>Verified source: <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/processing/messaging.py#L405">processing/messaging.py#L405</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/processing/lifecycle.py#L184">processing/lifecycle.py#L184</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/processing/lifecycle.py#L28">processing/lifecycle.py#L28</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/messaging.py#L16">media/messaging.py#L16</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/delivery/sql.py#L18">delivery/sql.py#L18</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/projections.py#L36">media/projections.py#L36</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/projections.py#L69">media/projections.py#L69</a></p></aside>
