-<aside class="notes"><b>w3-edit · NEW after s31</b><p>Read the left panel first. v1_jobs.edit calls v1_lifecycle.edit(session,storage,owner_id,parent_id,request,key). replay runs before parent validation; a key replay returns the prior Asset and invalid parent raises 409. Parent must be done with primary output. intake.stage commits a durable StagedObject. Copy holds parent and staged locks, streams GET bytes through a SHA-256-checked TemporaryFile, and PUTs sources/{owner}/{new_asset}/source. v1_lifecycle.pin_copied_source delegates to direct_intake.pin_copied_source; the version verification and SourceVersion insertion occur inside adoption. Derived Asset.source_asset_id points to parent. Asset + SourceVersion + optional RequestKey + submit outbox and staged-ledger removal commit together. Now read the right panel: EventBridge invokes MediaRepair and its publisher reserves/commits before SQS send and fences its ACK. API returns 202 before that later relay. Exceptions invoke discard_stage; uncertain writes retain cleanup authority. A concurrent RequestKey loser discards its own copy and replays the winner.</p><p>Sequence aliases: s=session, f=factory, cfg=settings, t=transport, e=envelope, jid/aid=Job/Attempt UUID, rid=reservation UUID, dir=temporary directory. These are argument values, not new API parameters. «module» lifelines denote real module executions; no OO controller classes are implied. Omitted callback internals are expanded in the linked W3 detail panels.</p><p>Verified source: <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/api/v1_jobs.py#L55">media/api/v1_jobs.py#L55</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L105">media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L105</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L145">media/services/v1_lifecycle.py#L145</a> <a href="https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/media/services/direct_intake.